Package: awwafwas
Title: American Water Works Association (AWWA) Free Water Audit Software (FWAS): data tools   
Version: 1.0.1
Authors@R: 
    person("Michael", "Thompson", , "michael.thompson@drbc.gov", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: The R code defines a function compile_FWAS that automates the extraction and compilation of 
    data from multiple versions of AWWA Free Water Audit Software (FWAS) reports, which are expected to be in 
    Excel (.xlsx) format. The function takes a directory path containing these reports as input, iteratively 
    reads each file, identifies its FWAS version (e.g., 6.0, 5.0, 4.1/4.2) by checking specific cells, and then 
    extracts relevant data points from various worksheets (e.g., "Start Page," "Worksheet," "Dashboard") 
    based on predefined indexing files. It consolidates this information into a single data frame, including 
    details like the original FWAS version, filename, compilation timestamp, and compiler's username, while 
    also flagging potential data quality issues like missing scores or negative water losses. Optionally, users 
    can specify a directory and filename to save the compiled data as a new Excel workbook.
